From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:20:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: PCI: qcom: Add endpoint-powered-off-in-suspend

Some boards carry an endpoint whose power sequencing is owned by an
agent the operating system does not control, and that agent removes the
endpoint's power while the system sleeps. On the Google Pixel 2 XL
(msm8998), the Easel coprocessor (Intel 8086:3140, the "Pixel Visual
Core") behind the single root port of pcie@1c00000 powers itself down
during the first system suspend and never returns on its own: the link
is dead on resume and stays dead until the device is fully power-cycled
by its own controller, outside the kernel's reach.

The host controller driver needs to know this: its link-down suspend
path powers the controller off and reinitializes the host on resume,
and on such boards that reinitialization runs against an absent link
partner (see the driver change for the measured consequences).

Describe the hardware fact with a boolean on the Root Port node: the
device downstream of this port is powered off in system suspend. The
property deliberately describes the endpoint's behaviour, not a driver
policy; what the OS does about it is the driver's decision.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-common.yaml        | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-common.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-common.yaml
index ab2509ec1c4b..22afb26450ff 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-common.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-common.yaml
@@ -111,6 +111,15 @@ patternProperties:
       phys:
         maxItems: 1
 
+      endpoint-powered-off-in-suspend:
+        type: boolean
+        description:
+          The device downstream of this Root Port is powered off while the
+          system is suspended, by an agent outside the operating system's
+          control (the device's own firmware or an external power
+          controller). The link will be down on resume and the device
+          cannot be brought back by link retraining alone.
+
     unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 required:
